# Agent Guide

## Read First

Before project work, read:

1. `docs/README.md`
2. The relevant spec or decision linked from `docs/README.md`

Use this file as a table of contents, not as a full instruction manual. Durable project knowledge should live in `docs/`.

## Project Structure

{% if backend_stack == 'rust' -%}
- `crates/` - Rust workspace crates, organized by layer and domain.
{% elif backend_stack == 'dotnet' -%}
- `backend/` - .NET API solution and tests.
{% endif -%}
{% if frontend_stack != 'none' -%}
- `{{ frontend_dir }}/` - {% if frontend_stack == 'astro' %}Astro frontend{% else %}Vite frontend{% endif %}.
{% endif -%}
- `docs/` - Product specs, technical specs, decisions, and repeatable tasks.
- `scripts/` - Local maintenance and validation scripts.
{% if include_api_contract | default(false) -%}
- `{% if backend_stack == 'dotnet' %}{{ dotnet_openapi_contract_path }}{% else %}{{ openapi_contract_path }}{% endif %}` - Committed OpenAPI contract.
- `{{ frontend_schema_path }}` - Generated frontend API schema types.
{% endif %}
## Scripts

Run write-mode formatting:

```bash
./scripts/format.sh
```

Run final validation:

```bash
./scripts/finalize.sh
```

`finalize.sh` is check-only and should not modify files. Run it before considering implementation work complete.

{% if include_layering_validator -%}
Architecture layering is enforced by `scripts/validate-layering.mjs` as part of `finalize.sh`. Update `docs/specs/architecture-layering-v0.1.md` before changing layer rules.

{% endif -%}
{% if include_api_contract | default(false) -%}
Regenerate backend OpenAPI and frontend API types:

```bash
./scripts/generate-api-contract.sh
```

`finalize.sh` checks that committed generated contracts are current. Do not hand-write frontend DTOs for backend API responses.

Before changing project conventions, validation scripts, architecture rules, generated schemas, or agent-facing docs, read `docs/specs/agent-governance-v0.1.md`.

{% endif -%}
For documentation, contract, and code alignment checks, use `docs/tasks/alignment-check.md`.

Run the local stack:

```bash
./scripts/dev.sh
```

Check a running local stack:

```bash
./scripts/check-health.sh
```

Run a temporary startup smoke check:

```bash
./scripts/smoke.sh
```

`smoke.sh` starts the configured local services, checks configured endpoints, and kills only the PIDs it started. Run it after changes to startup, routing, environment wiring, or cross-app integration.

## Development Commands

{% if backend_stack == 'rust' -%}
Backend:

```bash
cargo run -p {{ rust_api_package }}
cargo check --workspace
cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings
./scripts/check-rust-module-docs.sh
cargo test --workspace
```

{% elif backend_stack == 'dotnet' -%}
Backend:

```bash
dotnet run --project {{ dotnet_api_project_path }}
dotnet build {{ dotnet_solution_path }}
dotnet test {{ dotnet_solution_path }}
```

{% endif -%}
{% if frontend_stack != 'none' -%}
Frontend:

```bash
pnpm --dir {{ frontend_dir }} dev
pnpm --dir {{ frontend_dir }} build
{% if frontend_stack == 'astro' -%}
pnpm --dir {{ frontend_dir }} check
pnpm --dir {{ frontend_dir }} test
{% else -%}
pnpm --dir {{ frontend_dir }} lint
pnpm --dir {{ frontend_dir }} format:check
{% endif -%}
```

{% endif -%}
Markdown:

```bash
./scripts/lint-md.sh
```

## Repository Harness Principles

- Keep repository-local docs as the system of record.
- Prefer small indexed docs over one large instruction file.
- Add mechanical checks when a convention becomes important.
- Keep generated contracts current and committed when they are part of the workflow.
- When docs and code drift, update the stale artifact in the same change when feasible.
